  *       deadlocks). The caller always participates as a worker and joins
  *       before returning, so {@code flushDirty()} remains a durability
  *       barrier.</li>
- *   <li><b>Bounded dirty set:</b> at most {@link #MAX_DIRTY} files are
- *       tracked; the eldest is flushed inline (backpressure on the Moonrise
- *       I/O thread) when the bound is exceeded. Duplicates coalesce because
- *       the set is keyed by file identity.</li>
+ *   <li><b>Bounded dirty set, first-dirty order:</b> at most {@link #MAX_DIRTY}
+ *       files are tracked in a {@code LinkedHashMap} keyed by file identity
+ *       with first-dirty nanos; repeat marks do NOT reorder (minecraft-0017).
+ *       Exceeding the bound flushes the longest-unflushed file inline
+ *       (backpressure on the Moonrise I/O thread). DELIBERATE change from
+ *       least-recently-written victim to longest-unflushed; strictly more
+ *       correct.</li>
+ *   <li><b>Age-based flush:</b> {@code flushDirty()} flushes only files whose
+ *       first-dirty age {@code >=} global {@code flush-frequency} seconds
+ *       (minecraft-0017); younger files stay tracked. Eviction forces all.</li>
  *   <li><b>Unload eviction:</b> {@code RegionFileStorage.close()} calls
- *       {@link #evict(Path)}, which flushes remaining dirty files and drops
- *       the registry entry so worlds do not leak coordinators.</li>
+ *       {@link #evict(Path)}, which force-flushes remaining dirty files and
+ *       drops the registry entry so worlds do not leak coordinators.</li>
  * </ol>
  *
  * <p>Durability model: {@code LinearRegionFile.write()} marks the file via
  * {@code isMarkedToSave()}; {@code RegionFileStorage} reports each write to
- * {@link #markDirty}, and the actual bytes hit disk on the next
- * {@link #flushDirty()} (world save), bound-pressure flush, or eviction.
+ * {@link #markDirty} (first-dirty timestamp kept), and the actual bytes hit
+ * disk on the next age-eligible {@link #flushDirty()} (world save),
+ * bound-pressure flush, or forced eviction.
  * Polling uses the A3 contract ({@code isMarkedToSave()} is specified
  * non-consuming; the flag is cleared only after a successful flush).</p>
  */
@@ -81,11 +86,12 @@ public final class LinearFlushCoordinator {
     /**
